# Resibo client — environment TEMPLATE. Committed; carries names only.
#
# Everything here is PUBLIC. Vite inlines every VITE_-prefixed value into the
# JavaScript bundle the browser downloads, so a credential must never appear in
# a file like this one. See resibo-plan.md §8.
#
# No env file is required. Local development uses the /api proxy to the local
# backend on :8083; a production build uses the deployed API. See
# src/config/env.ts. The local backend may still use the shared live database;
# check its datasource before creating accounts.

# Base URL for the API, including the /api prefix.
#
# Leave unset for the environment-specific default. The local dev default is
# /api, proxied by Vite to localhost:8083; production defaults to the deployed
# API. To choose the local proxy explicitly:
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api
#
# Or name another origin explicitly:
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8083/api
#
# Set VITE_API_BASE_URL to the deployed host only when you intend to use live
# accounts from a development machine. Never add a credential to this file.
